Onest and DM Mono — the two typefaces the design specifies

Both are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The licence text of each is
bundled beside the font files, because OFL requires it to travel with every
copy of the Font Software, and the app ships them inside its resources.

Source:   https://github.com/google/fonts
Commit:   8e44913e4ff26fc997e6856c1ec40ff4791c98c5  (2026-09-10)

Onest
  Upstream:  https://github.com/simpals/onest
  Path:      ofl/onest/Onest[wght].ttf
  Version:   2.001
  Axis:      wght 100–900 (default 400) — one variable file covers every
             weight the design asks for, including the 650 of the headings,
             which no static instance ships.
  Renamed:   Onest-VariableFont_wght.ttf — the same file under the name
             Google Fonts' own download uses. The brackets in the upstream
             name are awkward in a build script and buy nothing.
  Copyright: 2021 The Onest Project Authors

DM Mono
  Upstream:  https://github.com/googlefonts/dm-mono
  Path:      ofl/dmmono/DMMono-{Light,Regular,Medium}.ttf
  Version:   1.000
  Copyright: 2020 The DM Mono Project Authors
  The three upright weights the design uses (300 / 400 / 500). The six italics
  upstream ships are not vendored: the design never sets a number in italic.

